Actually, re-reading: order §3.15 is explicit and seems to override the general contract vagueness. It says Retiro creates an entry in en_retirada (list). It does not impose at most one. And the order is the implementation contract. But the order also says if the contract has a rule with two incompatible implementations, report as AMBIGUEDAD and implement the most restrictive. So I'll report AMBIGÜEDAD for the "at most one pending withdrawal" and pick the restrictive reading: reject a second withdrawal while one is pending.

