AMBIGÜEDAD-2: Multiple simultaneous withdrawals per key. C-BON-05 says at most one, consolidation PENDING; order §4.2 models a list, §3.15 says "crea una entrada". Restrictive reading: reject a second Retiro while one is pending, with new error ErrRetiroPendiente. (Marked in code.)

AMBIGÜEDAD-3: Transferencia with Σ salidas > Σ entradas (negative fee) would silently mint and keep I-1 by inflating Emitido. Restrictive reading: require Σ salidas ≤ Σ entradas, else ErrSaldo. (Documented.)

AMBIGÜEDAD-4: Promotion vs. M_dep=0 (deposit active at h+M_dep). Step order (b) before (d) delays same-block maturity. Reading: a pending whose maturity ≤ current point is credited directly to activo at creation. Doesn't alter another rule.

AMBIGÜEDAD-5: I-7 literal statement vs CUT-H/CUT-W. Restrictive/consistent reading: a valid PoST block requires a terminal in its past (TRN-04+TRN-06); the literal "Φ falso ⇒" holds for CUT-HWΦ. For CUT-H/CUT-W, Φ is not part of TRN-04 by definition. Documented; tested structurally.

AMBIGÜEDAD-6: Coinbase position within block. Order says "coinbase primera"; blocks with coinbase not first. Reading: apply coinbase first regardless of list position (no new error), and at most one coinbase per block (else ErrEmision). Actually let me reconsider: maybe require exactly the order. Hmm. Let me just process the coinbase first and reject >1 coinbase. Document.

AMBIGÜEDAD-7: Missing error for structural violations (altura not increasing, peso<1, non-increasing slot). Reading: reuse ErrSlot for slot/peso/altura progression; ErrPow for pow_ok/trabajo. Document.

AMBIGÜEDAD-8: SEC-0 with sector txs / non-zero sector field. Reading: sector txs in SEC-0 → ErrFueraDeAlcanceV0; non-zero sector field ignored. Hmm, maybe better to reject non-zero sector in SEC-0 too. Let me document.

AMBIGÜEDAD-9: AltaSector before H_dep / in PoST. Reading: in PoST → ErrFueraDeAlcanceV0 (order §3.7); in PoW before H_dep → ErrDepositoTemprano. Document.

AMBIGÜEDAD-10: EvidenceTx in PoW → ErrOperacionFase (X-13); in PoST → ErrFueraDeAlcanceV0 (order §3.7). Document.

AMBIGÜEDAD-11: Deposit in PoST maturity. Order doesn't give PoST deposit maturity explicitly; reading: slot + M_dep_slots. Document.

AMBIGÜEDAD-12: Undo implemented as full snapshot of Estado (exact by construction). Document.

AMBIGÜEDAD-13: `seleccionar` validity of orphan blocks (parent absent). Reading: orphans ignored/not valid. Document.

Also maybe:
AMBIGÜEDAD-14: firma/authorization for Transferencia: firmante = dueño of each input. For Deposito: firmante = clave and owns inputs. For AltaSector: firmante=clave. For PruebaSector: firmante=owner. Document.

Let me also note the discrepancy that ORDEN §4.2 says error `ErrGenesis` for X-01 etc.

