`aplicar_post!`:
```julia
function aplicar_post!(E, B, P)
    # parent must be a terminal or a PoST block
    if E.fase == FasePoW
        E.terminal != -1 || return ErrSinTerminal
        B.padre == E.terminal || return ErrSinTerminal
        B.slot >= 1 || return ErrSlot
        E.fase = FasePoST
        E.s0 = 0
    else
        B.slot > E.slot || return ErrSlot
    end
    B.peso >= 1 || return ErrSlot
    # (b) promote
    r = promover!(E, P)
    r isa Err && return r
    # (c) producer guarantee
    g = get_garantia(E, B.productor)
    g.activo >= UInt64(P.q) || return ErrGarantia
    # SEC-A sector
    if P.sec == SECA
        reg = get(E.sectores, B.sector, nothing)
        reg === nothing && return ErrAutorizacion
        reg.P == B.productor || return ErrAutorizacion
        sector_activo(reg, E) || return ErrSectorInactivo
    end
    # (d) txs
    r2 = aplicar_txs!(E, B, P)
    r2 isa Err && return r2
    E.slot = B.slot
    E.bloque_raiz = B.id
    return nothing
end
```

Wait, for the transition block, `E.fase` is set to FasePoST before applying txs. Then txs like Deposito/Transferencia will use the PoST point (slot). Good.

But careful: `promover!` for the transition block should promote by slot (PoST). Since I set E.fase=PoST before promover!, good. But the producer guarantee check uses promotiones at the current slot. Good.

Hmm, but the order's step (b) for PoST uses `≤ s` (slot). For the transition block, its slot is B.slot. So pending with madura_en_slot ≤ B.slot promote. Good.

