Wait, but for the transition block we set E.fase=PoST and E.slot is still the parent's slot (0 for terminal). B.slot hasn't been assigned yet. So `punto = E.slot` would be 0, not B.slot. Bug! I need to use the block's point, not E.slot, for the promotion at the new block. Let me pass the point explicitly.

Let me refactor `promover!(E, punto)` where punto is the application point (B.altura for PoW, B.slot for PoST). For PoW, promote pendientes by altura; for PoST, by slot. I'll pass a boolean or use E.fase (set correctly before). Actually for PoW I can call `promover!(E, B.altura, false)`; for PoST `promover!(E, B.slot, true)`.

```julia
function promover!(E, punto::Int, es_post::Bool)
    for (k,g) in E.garantias
        nuevos = Pendiente[]
        restantes = Pendiente[]
        for p in g.pendientes
            if es_post
                if p.madura_en_slot != -1 && p.madura_en_slot <= punto
                    # promote
                    r = add_activo!(g, p.importe)
                    r isa Err && return r
                else
                    push!(restantes, p)
                end
            else
                if p.madura_en_altura != -1 && p.madura_en_altura <= punto
                    r = add_activo!(g, p.importe); r isa Err && return r
                else
                    push!(restantes, p)
                end
            end
        end
        g.pendientes = restantes
        # credits only in PoST
        if es_post
            restantesc = Pendiente[]
            for p in g.creditos
                if p.madura_en_slot != -1 && p.madura_en_slot <= punto
                    r = add_activo!(g,p.importe); r isa Err && return r
                else
                    push!(restantesc, p)
                end
            end
            g.creditos = restantesc
        end
    end
    return nothing
end
```

Hmm, for PoW promotions, deposits have both madura_en_altura and madura_en_slot. If we promote by altura in PoW, once promoted it's removed. Fine. But what if a deposit matured by slot before reaching PoW terminal? Can't happen since PoW has no slots. Fine.

But there's a subtle issue: In PoW, a pending deposit with madura_en_altura ≤ punto promotes. But what if its madura_en_altura > any future height because the terminal already happened at a lower height? Then in PoST, it promotes by slot. But its madura_en_slot = M_dep_slots. Good.

However, what about a deposit created in PoW with `madura_en_altura` > terminal height, but the PoST transition happens at slot 0 and we promote at slot = B.slot. If B.slot ≥ M_dep_slots, promotes. Good.

Now, `add_activo!` with checked_add.

#### aplicar_txs!

```julia
function aplicar_txs!(E, B, P)
    # compute tarifas
    tarifas = Int128(0)
    ncb = 0
    for tx in B.txs
        if tx.tipo == TxTransferencia
            # entradas - salidas
            ve = sum_valores_entradas(E, tx.entradas)  # can err
            vs = sum_valores_salidas(tx.salidas)
            tarifas += ve - vs
        elseif tx.tipo == TxCoinbase || tx.tipo == TxCoinbasePost
            ncb += 1
        end
    end
    ncb <= 1 || return ErrEmision
    # apply coinbase first
    orden = ... # coinbase first then others
    coinbase_pagada = UInt64(0)
    for tx in orden
        r = aplicar_tx!(E, B, P, tx, tarifas)
        r isa Err && return r
        if tx.tipo == TxCoinbase
            # sum salidas
            ...
        elseif tx.tipo == TxCoinbasePost
            coinbase_pagada = tx.importe
        end
    end
    # check coinbase limit
    subsidio = B.familia == PoW ? subsidio_pow(B.altura, P) : subsidio_post(B.slot, P)
    limite = subsidio + tarifas
    coinbase_pagada <= limite || return ErrEmision
    # update emitido
    E.emitido += Int128(coinbase_pagada) - tarifas
    ...
end
