Now `aplicar_pow!`:
```
function aplicar_pow!(E,B,P)
    E.fase == FasePoW || return (E.fase == FasePoST ? ErrPowTrasCorte : ErrGenesis)
    E.terminal == -1 || return ErrPowTrasCorte
    B.pow_ok || return ErrPow
    B.trabajo >= 1 || return ErrPow
    B.altura == E.altura + 1 || return ErrSlot
    r = promover!(E, B.altura, false); r isa Err && return r
    r = aplicar_txs!(E, B, P, B.altura); r isa Err && return r
    E.trabajo_acum += B.trabajo
    E.altura = B.altura
    E.bloque_raiz = B.id
    if es_terminal_condiciones(E, B, P)
        E.terminal = B.id
        E.altura_terminal = B.altura
    end
    return nothing
end
```

Wait, `B.altura == E.altura + 1`: at genesis, E.altura=0, so first PoW block must be altura 1. Good.

`aplicar_post!`:
```
function aplicar_post!(E,B,P)
    if E.fase == FasePoW
        E.terminal != -1 || return ErrSinTerminal
        B.padre == E.terminal || return ErrSinTerminal
        B.slot >= 1 || return ErrSlot
        E.fase = FasePoST
        E.s0 = 0
    elseif E.fase == FasePoST
        B.slot > E.slot || return ErrSlot
    else
        return ErrGenesis
    end
    B.peso >= 1 || return ErrSlot
    r = promover!(E, B.slot, true); r isa Err && return r
    g = get_garantia(E, B.productor)
    g.activo >= UInt64(P.q) || return ErrGarantia
    if P.sec == SECA
        reg = get(E.sectores, B.sector, nothing)
        reg === nothing && return ErrAutorizacion
        reg.P == B.productor || return ErrAutorizacion
        sector_activo(reg, E, B.slot) || return ErrSectorInactivo
    end
    r = aplicar_txs!(E, B, P, B.slot); r isa Err && return r
    E.slot = B.slot
    E.bloque_raiz = B.id
    return nothing
end
```

Wait, for the transition block, I set E.fase=PoST before `promover!`. But the sector active check uses E.fase PoST and E.altura_terminal. Good.

But there's an issue: for the transition block, `B.padre == E.terminal`. But `E.bloque_raiz` is the terminal. Should check `B.padre == E.bloque_raiz`? Actually, after applying the terminal T, E.bloque_raiz = T.id and E.terminal = T.id. A valid PoW state has bloque_raiz == terminal (since no valid PoW block after terminal). So B.padre == E.terminal suffices. But what if E is a PoW state that isn't a terminal? Then E.terminal=-1 → ErrSinTerminal. Good.

For a PoST block whose parent is a PoST block, we don't check B.padre == E.bloque_raiz. Should we? The caller (seleccionar) ensures the parent chain. For direct `aplicar` calls in tests, we construct correctly. I'll add a check `B.padre == E.bloque_raiz` maybe? But at transition, E.bloque_raiz = T.id = E.terminal. For PoST descendant, E.bloque_raiz = parent PoST id. So checking `B.padre == E.bloque_raiz` is a good consistency check. Error if mismatch? Hmm, no specified error. I'll skip to avoid inventing.

Actually, for `seleccionar`, `aplicar` is called with the parent's state (computed by applying the parent), so `B.padre` matches E.bloque_raiz by construction. Fine.

Now, the `sector_activo`:
```
function sector_activo(reg, E, punto)
    reg.prueba_en == -1 && return false
    reg.prueba_en > reg.plazo && return false
    if E.fase == FasePoST
        return reg.activa_en <= E.altura_terminal
    else
        return punto >= reg.activa_en
    end
end
```
Wait, in PoST, "si ya lo estaba en T". At the transition, E.altura_terminal is T's height. A sector is active at T if prueba ok and activa_en ≤ altura_terminal. Good. But at the transition block, E.fase was just set to PoST. Good.

For `phi`:
```
function phi(E, P)
    total = Int128(0)
    nq = 0
    for (_,g) in E.garantias
        total += Int128(g.activo)
        g.activo >= UInt64(P.q) && (nq += 1)
    end
    total >= P.S_min || return false
    nq >= P.K_min || return false
    if P.sec == SECA
        ns = 0
        for (_,reg) in E.sectores
            sector_activo(reg, E, punto_actual(E)) && (ns += 1)
        end
        ns >= P.C_min || return false
    end
    return true
end
```
`punto_actual(E) = E.fase==FasePoST ? E.slot : E.altura`. But for `es_terminal_condiciones`, E is in PoW; punto_actual=E.altura which was just set to B.altura. Good. Actually in aplicar_pow! I set E.altura = B.altura before checking terminal. Good.

