The issue: `sin1[2][end]` is the terminal state of the `sin_clave1` branch. In that branch, key 1 receives nothing (h=1 coinbase goes to key 2). But later coinbases go to `prod=1` by default (dst = prod when claves_extra is empty). So key 1 DOES receive later coinbases, and deposits them! So key 1 has garantía. Hence the transition by producer 1 is valid, not ErrGarantia.

To make key 1 have no garantía, I need to avoid crediting key 1 at all. The `sin_clave1` flag only changes h=1. Later coinbases go to prod=1. Let me set `claves_extra=[2]` so later coinbases go to key 2, and `sin_clave1=true`. Then key 1 never receives anything. Let me modify `historia_reorg` to use `claves_extra=[2]`.

